The upstream file credits NumPy/SVML's tanh algorithm; its BSD license is
also retained as SVML-hyperbolic-LICENSE.

Local modifications: scalarize the SIMD table lookup and Horner evaluation;
retain exact native float32 FMA in guarded normal ranges; replace hardware double operations and fused multiply-add with integer-backed
binary64 Metal operations; preserve NumPy's canonical NaN and target rounding.

The Apple scalar log10/sinh/cosh/tanh helpers are separate reconstructions of
installed macOS ARM64 operation sequences and numerical coefficients, not
represented as derivatives of the NumPy source or as a BSD Apple source port.
The private hyper_fma helper reuses stable_math64's exact arithmetic, including
Apache-2.0 ArrowMetal-derived final round/pack rules; see
ArrowMetal-stable-division-NOTICE and ArrowMetal-LICENSE.
